    {
     "type": "heading",
     "text": "Stop 2: The bond works both ways"
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "markdown": "Bonds work both ways: 7 + 3 = 10 and 3 + 7 = 10.\n\nTake away uses the bond too: 10 - 7 = 3.",
     "say": "Here is a secret. Bonds work both ways. Seven plus three is ten. And three plus seven is ten too. The numbers swap places but the total stays the same. And if we know seven plus three is ten, we know ten take away seven is three. One fact gives us a whole family of facts."
    },
